From: imanu <imanu86@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:41:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] OPUS-ENGINE-Scrivi la traccia di instradamento anche nelle
 finestre di verifica

Con --serve il motore decodifica solo con finestre di verifica, e --dump-routing era scritto soltanto da drive_pool (token singolo): una sessione servita lasciava la traccia vuota. drive_pool_multi scrive lo stesso record per ogni riga della finestra (bozze comprese, pesi a 0) e fa flush per strato, cosi' la traccia sopravvive a un motore chiuso bruscamente. Serve per costruire il profilo degli esperti dall'uso reale (tools/make_profile.py).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/program/generate.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/program/generate.cpp b/src/program/generate.cpp
index 0364a73..6ee4d28 100644
--- a/src/program/generate.cpp
+++ b/src/program/generate.cpp
@@ -513,6 +513,20 @@ void drive_pool_multi(void* user, const float* x_f, const int32_t* ids, int64_t
     strata::core::expert_pool_dispatch_multi(t->d, x_f, ids, n_tok, k, out);
     t->cpu_ms += std::chrono::duration<double, std::milli>(Clock::now() - a).count();
     ++t->calls;
+    // The routing trace in verify windows too (`--serve` decodes only through them, so a served session wrote an
+    // empty trace).  Same record as `drive_pool`, one per row of the window (drafts included: the cache serves them
+    // as well); the window carries no router weights here, so they are written as 0 - tools/make_profile.py skips
+    // them.  Flushed per layer: a served engine usually ends by being killed, and the trace must survive that.
+    if (t->routing != nullptr && layer >= 0 && layer < 48) {
+        static const float zeros[64] = {};
+        for (int64_t r = 0; r < n_tok; ++r) {
+            const int32_t rec[2] = {(int32_t) layer, (int32_t) k};
+            std::fwrite(rec, sizeof rec, 1, t->routing);
+            std::fwrite(ids + r * k, sizeof(int32_t), (size_t) k, t->routing);
+            std::fwrite(zeros, sizeof(float), (size_t) std::min<int64_t>(k, 64), t->routing);
+        }
+        std::fflush(t->routing);
+    }
 }
 
 /// Layer split: every verify stage shares one Drive (its counters, usage and failure flags); the GPU plan, the expert
